    <vann:example>
        :my-journal-article a fabio:JournalArticle ;
            prism:pageRange '145-162' .
    </vann:example>
    <ns:term_status xml:lang="en">stable</ns:term_status>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="http://prismstandard.org/namespaces/basic/2.0"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topDataProperty"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#AFRiskExplanation4">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://purl.org/heals/eo#scientificExplanation"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://purl.org/heals/eo#ContrastiveExplanation"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Example scientific and contrastive explanation of Atieno's AF risk assessment, provided to her clinician Dr Chebet.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>AF risk explanation 4</rdfs:label>
    <ep:isBasedOn rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#AFRiskAssessment1"/>
    <phmo:isConsumedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#DrChebet"/>
    <phmo:hasText>The hybrid Bayesian network classified Atieno's AF risk as present on 10 July 2026, with a calibrated probability of 0.64 against a decision threshold of 0.053. Hypertension is the input state that distinguishes this result from AF risk absent; it is an established risk factor for AF in the 2024 ESC guidelines for the management of AF.</phmo:hasText>
    <core:hasTimestamp rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTimeStamp">2026-07-10T14:30:00+03:00</core:hasTimestamp>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/phmo#BMI">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://purl.org/phmo#AnthropometricProperty"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdfs:label>BMI</rdfs:label>
    <rdfs:comment>An indicator of body density as determined by the relationship of body weight to body height. BMI = weight (kg)/height squared (m2).</rdfs:comment>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>UMLS:C1305855</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>Body mass index</oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#AFRiskExplanation2">
    <core:hasTimestamp rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTimeStamp">2026-07-10T14:30:00+03:00</core:hasTimestamp>
    <rdfs:comment>Example data explanation of Atieno's AF risk assessment, provided to her clinician Dr Chebet.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://purl.org/heals/eo#DataExplanation"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://purl.org/heals/eo#SafetyAndPerformanceExplanation"/>
    <rdfs:label>AF risk explanation 2</rdfs:label>
    <phmo:hasText>The assessment was made by a hybrid Bayesian network trained and tested on the MIMIC-IV dataset. It achieved an AUROC of 0.82, a recall of 0.89, and a specificity of 0.58 at its decision threshold of 0.053.</phmo:hasText>
    <ep:isBasedOn rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#AFRiskAssessment1"/>
    <phmo:isConsumedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#DrChebet"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N71361b4195124bbd92ac1ad951eea44a">
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0000900"/>
    <oboInOwl:hasDbXref>NCIT:C38053</oboInOwl:hasDbXref>
    <owl:annotatedTarget>A procedure that displays the electrical activity of the heart.</owl:annotatedTarget>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/IAO_0000115"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/heals/eo#CounterfactualExplanation">
    <dcterms:source>Chari, S., Seneviratne, O., Ghalwash, M., Shirai, S., Gruen, D. M., Meyer, P., Chakraborty, P., &amp; McGuinness, D. L. (2024). Explanation Ontology: A general-purpose, semantic representation for supporting user-centered explanations. Semantic Web. https://doi.org/10.3233/SW-233282</dcterms:source>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://purl.org/heals/eo"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Addresses the question of what solutions would have been obtained with a different set of inputs than those used.</rdfs:comment>
    <skos:example>What if input A was over 1000?</skos:example>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
    <skos:scopeNote>Is there a different set of inputs that can be considered? If so what is the alternate ‘system recommendation’?</skos:scopeNote>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="http://linkedu.eu/dedalo/explanationPattern.owl#Explanation"/>
    <rdfs:label>Counterfactual explanation</rdfs:label>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/phmo#hasResponseIntervention">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <owl:inverseOf rdf:resource="http://purl.org/phmo#isInResponseTo"/>
