  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://purl.org/heals/eo#DataExplanation">
    <skos:example>How it has been used in a particular decision?</skos:example>
    <skos:example>How has the data been used to train the ML model?</skos:example>
    <skos:example>What the data is?</skos:example>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy rdf:resource="https://purl.org/heals/eo"/>
    <dcterms:source>Chari, S., Seneviratne, O., Ghalwash, M., Shirai, S., Gruen, D. M., Meyer, P., Chakraborty, P., &amp; McGuinness, D. L. (2024). Explanation Ontology: A general-purpose, semantic representation for supporting user-centered explanations. Semantic Web. https://doi.org/10.3233/SW-233282</dcterms:source>
    <rdfs:subClassOf rdf:resource="https://purl.org/heals/eo#SafetyAndPerformanceExplanation"/>
    <skos:scopeNote>Is there a ‘system recommendation’ from an ‘AI method’ that has as input, a ‘dataset’ or part of it? Is there a ‘system recommendation’ that includes ‘object records’ that are used to train / test the ‘AI method’?</skos:scopeNote>
    <rdfs:comment>Focuses on what the data is and how it has been used in a particular decision, as well as what data and how it has been used to train and test the ML model. This type of explanation can help users understand the influence of data on decisions.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Data explanation</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"/>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/title">
    <rdfs:label xml:lang="en">title</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty"/>
    <rdfs:domain rdf:resource="http://purl.org/phmo#Publication"/>
    <rdfs:range rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string"/>
    <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">A name given to a resource.  Typically, the title will be the name by which the resource is formally known.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://purl.org/afmo#InterventionExplanation2">
    <phmo:hasText>Dr Chebet has approved alcohol counselling for you. Studies show that counselling helps people reduce how much they drink, and drinking less lowers your risk of atrial fibrillation (AF).</phmo:hasText>
    <core:hasTimestamp rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#dateTimeStamp">2026-09-21T19:30:00+03:00</core:hasTimestamp>
    <rdfs:comment>Example scientific explanation of the recommendation of alcoholism counselling, provided to Atieno.</rdfs:comment>
    <rdfs:label>Intervention explanation 2</rdfs:label>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="https://purl.org/heals/eo#scientificExplanation"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#NamedIndividual"/>
    <ep:isBasedOn rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#HealthIntervention2"/>
    <phmo:isConsumedBy rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#Atieno"/>
  </rdf:Description>
