  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="N83eebd55206e4ef78a8dae55e77b1e5e">
    <owl:annotatedSource rdf:resource="http://purl.org/afmo#SmokingStatus"/>
    <rdfs:isDefinedBy>https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/nhis/tobacco/tobacco_recodes.htm#anchor_1557516509294 and the New Zealand Ministry of Health https://www.health.govt.nz/our-work/preventative-health-wellness/tobacco-control/tobacco-control-information-practitioners/definitions-smoking-status.

- Smoker (a.k.a current smoker): a person who has smoked more than 100 cigarettes (including hand rolled cigarettes, cigars, cigarillos etc) in their lifetime and has smoked in the last 28 days. Includes daily and non-daily/social smokers.
- Non-smoker: composed of two groups: former smoker and never smoker.
   - Former smoker: a person who has smoked more than 100 cigarettes in their lifetime but has not smoked in the last 28 days. The international convention is to treat someone as an ex-smoker once they have been smokefree for one month (at least 28 days).
   - Never smoker: a person who has not smoked more than 100 cigarettes in their lifetime and does not currently smoke.

Dagfinn et al. (2018) noted that there is reduced risk of AF among former smokers compared to current smokers, but further research is needed to determine if the risk at some point reaches that of never smokers.</rdfs:isDefinedBy>
    <owl:annotatedTarget xml:lang="en">A person's cigarette (tobacco) smoking behaviour.</owl:annotatedTarget>
    <owl:annotatedProperty rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Axiom"/>
  </rdf:Description>
